sn45.180:2.4 | S: These are the five higher fetters. | T: …
sn45.180:2.5 | S: The noble eightfold path should be developed for the direct knowledge, complete understanding, finishing, and giving up of these five higher fetters. | T: The Noble Eightfold Path is to be developed for direct knowledge of these five higher fetters, for the full understanding of them, for their utter destruction, for their abandoning.
sn45.180:2.6 | S: What is the noble eightfold path? | T: “What Noble Eightfold Path?
sn45.180:2.7 | S: It’s when a mendicant develops right view, right purpose, right speech, right action, right livelihood, right effort, right mindfulness, and right immersion, which culminate in the removal of greed, hate, and delusion …” | T: Here, bhikkhus, a bhikkhu develops right view … right concentration, which has as its final goal the removal of lust, the removal of hatred, the removal of delusion …
sn45.180:2.8 | S: “… whose objective, destination, and culmination is freedom from death …” | T: which has the Deathless as its ground, the Deathless as its destination, the Deathless as its final goal …
sn45.180:2.9 | S: “… which slant, slope, and incline to extinguishment. | T: which slants, slopes, and inclines towards Nibbāna.
sn45.180:2.10 | S: This is the noble eightfold path that should be developed for the direct knowledge, complete understanding, finishing, and giving up of these five higher fetters.” | T: This Noble Eightfold Path is to be developed for direct knowledge of these five higher fetters, for the full understanding of them, for their utter destruction, for their abandoning.”
sn45.180:2.11 | P: Dasamaṁ. | T: (none)
sn45.180:2.12 | P: Oghavaggo aṭṭhamo. | T: (none)
sn45.180:3.0 | P: Tassuddānaṁ | T: (none)
sn45.180:3.1 | P: Ogho yogo upādānaṁ, | T: (none)
sn45.180:3.2 | P: ganthaṁ anusayena ca; | T: (none)
sn45.180:3.3 | P: Kāmaguṇā nīvaraṇaṁ, | T: (none)
sn45.180:3.4 | P: khandhā oruddhambhāgiyāti. | T: (none)
sn45.180:4.0 | P: vagguddānaṁ | T: (none)
sn45.180:4.1 | P: Avijjāvaggo paṭhamo, | T: (none)
